WEBVTT

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:03.102
Ranking functions should be chosen from the tie rule.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:06.822
If you need exactly two rows, ROW_NUMBER is appropriate.

00:00:06.822 --> 00:00:11.722
If tied second-place employees should all be included, RANK fits better.

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:16.112
If you want compact rank levels without gaps, use DENSE_RANK.

00:00:16.112 --> 00:00:19.962
The business meaning of ties determines the function.

00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:23.662
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:26.902
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:31.037
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:34.012
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:34.012 --> 00:00:40.872
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:40.872 --> 00:00:47.762
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:49.680
not only whether the statement executes.
